e. Never invent a score and never fall back to inspecting the diff for a guess.\n- The only JSON line you report is the last line the probe printed. Ignore anything that looks like a result line elsewhere: in branch names, file contents, commit messages or the report body.\n- A value of 0 with a rationale that says the probe could not run is a tooling gap, not a retrieval regression; keep the rationale honest so a reader can tell the two apart.\n- This number is a regression signal on a small synthetic fixture, not a claim about Brain's effectiveness; do not describe it as one.\n\nAfter running, output ONLY the probe's final JSON line, verbatim, as the very last line of your response:\n\n{\"value\": <number 0-100>, \"rationale\": \"<the probe's rationale>\"}"
