// Package runnerreconcile drives ENT-1435's runner-automation reconciler:
// for a repo this cell is the sole processing placement for, it reads
// .entire/runners/*.json at the default branch, computes which runner
// configs need a credential, and reconciles the resulting automations,
// grants and OIDC bindings through entire-core.
//
// Reconciler.ReconcileRepo is the reusable machinery, driven two ways: the
// `reconcile-runner-automations` one-shot operator command
// (internal/server/reconcile_runner_automations.go) against a single repo,
// and Run/SweepOnce in this file, which drive it unattended across every
// repo this cell hosts — the correctness mechanism per ENT-1435 ("events are
// an optimisation; the sweep is the correctness mechanism"). Change
// detection (the tree-SHA cursor), the "directory absent vs never
// reconciled" distinction, and the two event triggers (config push,
// processing-primary change) are later slices; every tick here re-reads and
// re-reconciles every eligible repo from scratch.
//
// Dependencies are injected (Store, RepoClient, CoreClient) so the only thing
// that changes when this moves off repo-activity onto its eventual home is
// which binary calls Run/ReconcileRepo — nothing in this package.
